        <h1>LeetCode 3963: Create Grid With Exactly One Path (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given two integers m and n, representing the number of rows and columns, build any m x n
                grid made of '.' (free cells) and '#' (obstacles) that has exactly one valid path from the
                top-left cell to the bottom-right cell. A valid path uses only free cells and moves either
                right or down at each step.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: m = 2, n = 3<br>
                Output: ["..#","#.."]<br>
                Explanation: The only valid path is (0,0) → (0,1) → (1,1) → (1,2).
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    vector&lt;string&gt; createGrid(int rows, int cols) {
        vector&lt;string&gt; matrix(rows, string(cols - 1, '#') + ".");
        matrix[0] = string(cols, '.');
        return matrix;
    }
};</code></pre>
